The grid is a list of 1, 2, 3, and 4.
The height is 2.
The width is 2.
The top is 0.
The front is 0.
The side is 0.
For every line from 0 to height minus 1.
The rowbest is 0.
For every column from 0 to width minus 1.
The amount is item (line times width plus column) of grid.
If amount is more than 0, add 1 to top.
If amount is more than rowbest, set rowbest to amount.
If column is width minus 1, add rowbest to front.

For every column from 0 to width minus 1.
The columnbest is 0.
For every line from 0 to height minus 1.
The amount is item (line times width plus column) of grid.
If amount is more than columnbest, set columnbest to amount.
If line is height minus 1, add columnbest to side.

The area is top plus front plus side.
Show area.
